          "channel": "Ryan Carniato",
          "description": "Dominic Gannaway, creator of InfernoJS, former React Core Team member, Compiler wizard, and all-around great guy, joins us this week to talk about his latest work bringing Fine-Grained Reactivity to Svelte 5.\n\n[0:00] Preamble\n[7:45] Welcome Dominic Gannaway & Early History\n[14:30] Dominic's Early Web Dev Journey \n[21:00] Inferno.js\n[31:45] What Made Inferno Fast?\n[37:30] Working at Facebook\n[47:00] Prepack \n[54:45] React Hooks & react-compiler \n[1:03:45] Lexical\n[1:10:30] Octane & Svelte 5 \n[1:17:00] Runes\n[1:24:00] Properly Exposing Signals in an API\n[1:36:30] CODE: Svelte 5 Playground & Compilation Output\n[1:51:15] Possible Future Improvements to Svelte\n[1:57:30] Q & A: Flow? JSDoc? TypeScript? Time Zones?\n[2:04:00] Q & A: Virtual DOM? Runes & Reactivity?\n[2:09:15] Q & A: Signals Spec? Community Response?\n[2:15:00] Q & A: SvelteKit? Production Ready?\n[2:20:00] Dominic's Parting Notes & Intermission\n[2:30:00] Signal Syntax & Compilation\n[2:46:15] Signals in the DOM & Benefits of VDOM\n[2:55:00] This Week in JavaScript: Fabio Spampinato - Signal Tweet\n[3:09:00] TWiJ: Solid 1.8 Release & Hydration Warnings\n[3:21:15] TWiJ: Template Cloning, Compilation, and Cost of Abstraction\n[3:31:30] TWiJ: React Server Components as NPM Packages & Serialization\n[3:42:00] TWiJ: Musing on Server Component Designs\n[4:02:30] TWiJ: DHH - \"No-Build\"\n[4:18:45] TWiJ: Andrew Clark - RSC's & HTMX\n[4:26:00] TWiJ: The Cycle of Progress\n[4:34:15] TWiJ: The Framework Reactivity Graph\n[4:43:45] TWiJ: Thinking Locally with Signals\n[5:12:15] TWiJ: Fresh 1.5\n[5:17:15] Conclusion\n\nThanks to @zombiefacesupreme for the timestamps.",
